        <content type="html" xml:base="https://rustdelhi.in/events/20250719/">&lt;p&gt;Hi folks, Rust Delhi hosted meetup on Saturday, July 19, 2025. It was a fantastic event that brought together Rust enthusiasts to share their experiences and discuss the future of the Rust Delhi community.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The venue was graciously provided by our friends at &lt;a rel=&quot;noopener nofollow noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;essentia.dev&quot;&gt;essentia.dev&lt;&#x2F;a&gt;!&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;event-agenda&quot;&gt;Event Agenda:&lt;&#x2F;h3&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kickstarting Rust Delhi.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;“Rust 101 and Poem crate for OpenAPI Compatibility” by Guinnes Singh.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&quot;Setting up dev environment for Rust in linux kernel&quot; by Shresth Prasad.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&quot;POSIX Message Queues with Rust&quot; by Tanveer Raza.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&quot;Designing Microprocessors with Rust&quot; by Sameer.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Networking + Food.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product pitches by Aftershoot, YRAL and EMBETTER TECHNOLOGIES.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hiring and Pitching. Open to anyone hiring for a Rust role, looking for a Rust role, or otherwise.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
